From b13e1f2cf7a07ceaa1ee2d492a52693f26e988af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Payrard?= <cognominal@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:42:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat: hover help stands aside for the leader menu

While the leader or one of its menus waits for a key, the explainer is
not drawn: the menu is the next thing read, and two overlays on one
screen compete for the same glance. Moving the pointer under the menu
does not change the target, so the explainer comes back on the part it
left when the menu closes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/KEYBINDINGS.md        |  4 +++-
 e2e/tui/hover_help_test.go | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 internal/app/hover_help.go | 10 +++++++---
 3 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

